# Lines of code

https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L276-L292
https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L294-L314


# Vulnerability details

## Impact

This can cause users to incur higher fees than expected and have their CDPs show a greater debt than the actual eBTC received.

## Proof of Concept

Looking at both the [`_openCdpForCallback`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L276-L292) and [`_adjustCdpCallback`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-06-badger/blob/9173558ee1ac8a78a7ae0a39b97b50ff0dd9e0f8/ebtc-zap-router/src/LeverageZapRouterBase.sol#L294-L314) functions,the fee is calculated and deducted from the minted eBTC, but the full amount is still considered as debt in the CDP. This results in the CDP reflecting a higher debt than the actual eBTC received by the user.



```solidity
function _openCdpForCallback(bytes memory data) internal override {
    if (zapFeeBPS > 0) {
        OpenCdpForOperation memory flData = abi.decode(data, (OpenCdpForOperation));

        bytes32 _cdpId = borrowerOperations.openCdpFor(
            flData.eBTCToMint,
            flData._upperHint,
            flData._lowerHint,
            flData.stETHToDeposit,
            flData.borrower
        );

        IERC20(address(ebtcToken)).safeTransfer(zapFeeReceiver, flData.eBTCToMint * zapFeeBPS / BPS);
    } else {
        super._openCdpForCallback(data);
    }
}
```



```solidity
function _adjustCdpCallback(bytes memory data) internal override {
    if (zapFeeBPS > 0) {
        AdjustCdpOperation memory flData = abi.decode(data, (AdjustCdpOperation));

        borrowerOperations.adjustCdpWithColl(
            flData._cdpId,
            flData._stEthBalanceDecrease,
            flData._EBTCChange,
            flData._isDebtIncrease,
            flData._upperHint,
            flData._lowerHint,
            flData._stEthBalanceIncrease
        );

        if (flData._isDebtIncrease) {
            IERC20(address(ebtcToken)).safeTransfer(zapFeeReceiver, flData._EBTCChange * zapFeeBPS / BPS);
        }
    } else {
        super._adjustCdpCallback(data);
    }
}
```

## Tools Used

Manual code review.

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

The fee should be deducted from the minted eBTC before it is added to the CDP debt. This ensures that the CDP debt accurately reflects the actual eBTC received by the user.




