    uint256 _deposit = stEth.balanceOf(address(this)) - _balBefore;
    return _deposit;
}
```

In the above function, the external call is made using ```call{value: _initialETH}("")``` without checking the success of the operation. 

## Tools Used
Manual review.
## Recommended Mitigation Steps

To mitigate this issue, the function should be modified to check the return value of the external call and revert if the call fails. Here is the recommended change:

```sol
function _depositRawEthIntoLido(uint256 _initialETH) internal returns (uint256) {
    uint256 _balBefore = stEth.balanceOf(address(this));
